            "created_at": "2025-08-22T08:28:08.948485+00:00",
            "notes": "Some options between powers, so here's some text to explain them:\n- [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68): What I *almost always* choose, as with your CDR (which is going to get higher) alongside [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b) this will really speed up getting your ult, and combines well with the next power you'll be getting. If the enemy team doesn't really have effects you can cleanse, then if you and/or your teammates get [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8), that also counts as something you can cleanse, and all you need to do is take any form of damage!\n- [Leaf on the Wind](item_b64de259-d122-407d-a7e4-9d7267310704): For even more healing, and spreads the passive buffs to more of your team. If the enemies don't really have anything for [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68), and you don't think your team will get [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8), then this is a decent power choice. However, I rarely see this in late-game, as items like [El-sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100), [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) and [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) all count as effects you can cleanse. \n\nNothing special about the item choices this round, we finally have everything we wanted, from now on out it's icing on the cake",
