        {
            "id": "40c0d5bd-282b-4318-821b-2344fc5ec3bc",
            "build_id": "45467dc5-dd10-4ada-ba0d-e745d7af4c57",
            "round_number": 7,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-22T08:28:08.948485+00:00",
            "notes": "## POWERS:\n[Crossing Guard](item_bb5252fd-fc6b-4dce-a60a-21b0a0add68f)'s slow is NOT to be underestimated. 50% reduction is like moving in molasses. That said, if you didn't take [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68) in round 5, this won't be as useful for you as you won't be getting as many kitsunes, so you might want to take that now if you haven't yet. \n\nAs well as the round 5 choices, [Clone Conjuration](item_6c9f6be1-ab29-4f46-af24-34e4835f9af3) is another option if there's still no one on the enemy team with debuffs, since the clone's HP is based off of AP, and you have a decent amount. If you never took [Supported Shooting](item_4a084906-0fcd-4158-9a4b-763a69d0b198), and don't want to, this is what I'd probably go with, though [Leaf on the Wind](item_b64de259-d122-407d-a7e4-9d7267310704) is fine too. \n\n## ITEMS: \nA *LOT* of options as to what our final item slot will be, so here's another wall of text to explain them:\n- [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b): The straight up WP option. I know this seems a little silly given this is an AP build, but this'll give you a good boost to your regular ofuda, (as well as kunai), which you're using anyways for the passive buffs.\n- [Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48): If you're hitting yourself with your suzu more often than not, then this item becomes less needed. But, the AS and MS on it is nice. \n- [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8): As said in the previous round notes, this is a good item to mix with [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68) if the enemy team doesn't really have any debuffs for you to cleanse. It's also a decent survival item regardless. \n- [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98): With this, you'll have 40% cooldown reduction, which is awesome. More TPs so more heals, and more suzus so more buffs, overhealth *and* kitsunes. The 3% healing doesn't do too much for you, but it's not bad either. \n- [Our Bikes](item_d9fa8542-237e-49d5-b6a1-4e910d5c777f): Only take this item if you have [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68). That said, with 70% AP, this means your allies will heal 135 hp/s during kitsune rush, as well as your enemies being slowed by 50%. This is great for your team, and terrible for the enemies. \n- [Teamwork Toolkit](item_d56fb90c-cbe6-4ad5-8475-0ce920f92a3f): I removed this for [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448), since I think the 10% CDR is worth the trade, but if you don't have enough for two purples, then you can replace [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) with this again to take something else, or add this on if you want that bit of move speed for your team. Though, if you have the cash, I'd recommend taking another purple, as IMO they're generally more worth it.\n\nIf you're really short on cash, then both [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) and [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f) are what I go for in later rounds. They buff your heals, and you get a bit of CDR. \n\nOr, a less complicated TL;DR: if you have [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68) then take [Our Bikes](item_d9fa8542-237e-49d5-b6a1-4e910d5c777f), or [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) if the enemy team doesn't have any debuffs. Else, [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b) or [Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48) are good choices, or [Teamwork Toolkit](item_d56fb90c-cbe6-4ad5-8475-0ce920f92a3f) if you're low on cash. [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) is decent if you want higher cooldown reduction.",
